<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's MKB cuts prime lending rate to 24.50 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary's MKB cuts prime lending rate to 24.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB) said on Friday it will cut its prime lending rate on forint loans to 24.50 percent from 25.00 percent, effective September 9.</p>
<p>MKB is majority-owned by Germany's Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
